 "headline": "“VERY cool goodie package” - Brian Michael Bendis",
 "intro": "To celebrate the debut of Marvel Studios’ first live-action series, IHC conceptualized a custom at-home viewing kit.",
 "introPieces": [
  {
   "type": "introGallery",
   "media": [
    {
     "type": "image",
     "src": "/images/66df45a32db05ef1a5da080d_Case-Studies-_-Wandavision-_-General-_-Main-Gallery-_-Display-p-1600.webp",
     "alt": ""
    }
   ],
   "html": "<p>WandaVision was the perfect show for Marvel Studios to launch their new wave of content on Disney+. Celebrating the history of TV, the series struck a cord for an at-home viewing audience stuck indoors.</p>\n<p>Inspired by the show, we pitched a vintage TV dinner themed mailer, reminiscent of the classic sitcom era in which this story takes place. The goal was to give audiences the most premium at-home experience watching the series debut.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "The campaign",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>Disney+ shipped out over 1,400 kits to talent, influencers, and press through a Postmates partnership. A social media contest gave fans a chance to score a box as well. The campaign garnered press from Deadline and generated massive buzz among key cultural tastemakers.</p>",
     "right": "<p>Led by unboxing videos featuring Paul Betany (Vision), press and influencers were ecstatic to receive the gift boxes. Disney incorporated the campaign into their overarching global marketing plan.</p>"
    },
